{
	"name": "Blossom Ray",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/environment/creatures/fish-spotted-orange.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Resembling Tiny pastel-colored stingrays that fly through the air rather than water, blossom rays are typically found in groves of flowering trees, where they feed off of nectar, much like bees or butterflies. Curiously enough, the color of a blossom ray usually corresponds to the color of flowers they feed off of. Many people claim that watching blossom rays is inherently soothing. Adventurers who spend 30 minutes observing these rays in their natural habitat receive the benefits of a short rest.</p>",
